# ad-hoc test files that hit the network / hang under pytest
# raw `env` dump — contains tokens/passwords, never commit
# ── Generated run artifacts (system + eval harness) ──
# ── OS junk ──
# ── Python bytecode / caches ──
# ── Secrets ──
# ── Session scratch (screenshots, throwaway scripts, ad-hoc test files) ──
# ── Tooling / agent scratch ──
# ── Virtual envs ──
*$py.class
*.db
*.log
*.png
*.py[cod]
*.sqlite
.DS_Store
.DS_Store?
.agents/
.cache/
.claude/
.env
.env.*
# Must follow .env.* — gitignore takes the LAST matching pattern, so a negation
# placed above it has no effect and the template stops shipping on a fresh init.
!.env.example
.mypy_cache/
.playwright-mcp/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.superpowers/
.venv/
